// Max HP = ((((Level * Class HP per Level) + ((Base Stam + Bonus Stam) * Stam Multiplier))) - Offset) + Bonus HP

[Gate Switch Fix]
author=Switz0018
//The Drundar Arena Gate can be opened early by saving and exiting the game to menu.
//Upon loading the save, the game ADDS your saved gates to the value in memory.
//The memory used for this data is not cleared upon exit.
//Instead of ADDING, SET the value.

[Difficulty Changes]
author=Switz0018
description=Modify how difficulty is calculated.
// To fully understand how difficulty is calculated,
// we need to know what factors are used, and how.
// Adv. uses the same equation, without the multiplier.
// WorldDifficulty = ((Zone Difficulty + 2) * Difficulty Multiplier) + Base Difficulty
patch=3,EE,201E5B80,extended,24840006 // Add 6 to Zone Difficulty instead of 2.
patch=3,EE,101E5BCC,extended,00003F80 // Cour, 1.0
patch=3,EE,101E5BF0,extended,00003FA0 // Champ, 1.25
patch=3,EE,101E5C10,extended,00003FC0 // Lege, 1.5
patch=3,EE,101E5C30,extended,00003FE0 // Epic, 1.75

[Experience Rewards]
//XP is calculated in a few ways.
//XP rewards use an individually calculated XP value divided by player level.
//The result is then passed into powf with 1.4 as an exponent. The result of this is then multiplied by 0.75.
//This is the main calculation: 0.75(powf((x/y),1.4))
//fVar21 = powf(*(float *)(this + 0xd8) / (float)iVar4,1.4);
//iVar4 = (int)((float)(int)fVar21 * 0.75);
//Some further math is performed to reward XP to multiple players. Singleplayer ends here.
//In multiplayer, XP is always rewarded in order P1 -> P4.
//The player to land the killing blow is rewarded more XP than everyone else.
//A flag is set to identify which player has the killing blow, and is checked for each time we iterate the loop.
//The player with the killing blow gets 60% of the XP. Every other player gets 40%. Dead players get 20% (half).
//Everything is converted to int for rounding during the process. 125.206 becomes 125, 93.75 becomes 93, etc.
//Finally we have: KB = 0.6(0.75(powf((creature_xp/player_level),1.4))), PX = 0.4(0.75(powf((creature_xp/player_level),1.4)))
//Before XP is rewarded, a secondary check is done.
//The game tests the XP to rewarded against the difference in XP between the next two levels.
//(Level+2 XP Cost) - (Level+1 XP Cost)
//The lesser of the two values is rewarded.
//at pc -> 001120E4 s0 is equal to the XP to be rewarded.
//Multiple hardcoded factors can be changed to adjust the reward.
patch=3,EE,20111E88,extended,3C013F99 // 3FB3* (1.4)    | 3F99* (1.2)
patch=3,EE,20111E8C,extended,3421999A // *3333          | *999A
patch=3,EE,20111FDC,extended,3C013EA4 // 3F40 (0.75)    | 3EA3 (0.32)
patch=3,EE,2011203C,extended,3C013F19 // 3F19* (0.6)
patch=3,EE,20112040,extended,34219999 // *9999
patch=3,EE,20112050,extended,3C013ECC // 3ECC* (0.4)
patch=3,EE,20112054,extended,3421CCCC // *CCCC

